From 10fbc39cf57220eb93f61ce282d7561750f8d29d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DL6ER <dl6er@dl6er.de>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:52:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Return an empty block from blockdata_alloc() for zero length.

738c049 turned the allocation loop in blockdata_alloc_real() from
do/while into for, so a zero length now returns NULL. find_soa() and
extract_addresses() start the chain for an RR with
blockdata_alloc(NULL, 0) and fill it with blockdata_expand(), so they
now fail on every SOA and every RR that is not an address, e.g., MX,
SRV, or SVCB, and those answers are no longer cached. A zero-length
RR also no longer survives cache_recv_insert().

Allocate one empty block for zero length, as before.

Signed-off-by: DL6ER <dl6er@dl6er.de>

Upstream: https://thekelleys.org.uk/gitweb/?p=dnsmasq.git;a=commit;h=10fbc39cf57220eb93f61ce282d7561750f8d29d
---
 src/blockdata.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/blockdata.c b/src/blockdata.c
index a7ffadba..0414bf09 100644
--- a/src/blockdata.c
+++ b/src/blockdata.c
@@ -91,6 +91,11 @@ static struct blockdata *blockdata_alloc_real(int fd, char *data, size_t len)
   struct blockdata **prev = &ret;
   size_t blen;
   int fail;
+
+  /* Zero length still gives one empty block, blockdata_alloc(NULL, 0)
+     is how callers start a chain to add to with blockdata_expand(). */
+  if (len == 0)
+    return new_block();
   
   for (fail = 0; len != 0; len -= blen)
     {
@@ -252,10 +257,9 @@ void blockdata_write(struct blockdata *block, size_t len, int fd)
     }
 }
 
-/* NOTE: this can fail (NULL return) for three possible reasons.
-   1) len == 0 - trivial
-   2) end of stream. 
-   3) malloc failure when allocating blocks.
+/* NOTE: this can fail (NULL return) for two possible reasons.
+   1) end of stream. 
+   2) malloc failure when allocating blocks.
 
    Unless EOF is encountered, len octets will always be read from the stream,
    even in memory allocation fails.
